            <ArticleTitle>[A rare clinical case: myocardial infarction caused by coronary artery occlusion by cancer cells].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>631-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rare clinical case of myocardial infarction, conditioned by neoplasmal obturation of coronary artery, is presented in the article. Primary nidus of the neoplasmal growth was in 3 and 4 segments of the lung. Tumor penetrated pleura, pericardium, epicardium and infiltrated wall of the circumflex branch and formed neoplasmal thrombus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
